WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.807
Welcome to Module 3 of the
Ticket-to-Machine learning path:

2
00:00:03.807 --> 00:00:05.450
one writer per attribute.

3
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.809
This module follows the guide's Gate 2,

4
00:00:07.809 --> 00:00:12.070
which settles two decisions on
paper before anything is connected:

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.788
who writes each attribute, and which
system approves each authority class.

6
00:00:16.788 --> 00:00:20.190
Then you'll use the developer
workbook's Chapter 08 check,

7
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.824
which reads two provisioning
configurations, Entra inbound provisioning's

8
00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:28.588
and SailPoint's, and reports every
attribute both of them write.

9
00:00:28.588 --> 00:00:32.435
You'll run it on fictional exports,
add an alias, and see why the

10
00:00:32.435 --> 00:00:36.960
alias list and the directory name
are inputs a reviewer has to confirm.
